{
  "_name": "t72_anti_spam_gateway_relay_exempt",
  "_desc": "Fix-2 regression (gateway cross-layer forwards are exempt from the §10a originator throttle). l4_sender sends THREE cross-layer messages to l5_target (key 0xCAFE0000) via gw_4, which bridges L4->L5. On the target layer gw_4 re-injects each message with origin=self and no preceding CTS, so under the OLD R-C metric its forwards look like fresh originations: l5_helper (the next hop, originator_max_per_window=2) would observe gw_4's 3 distinct forwards and throttle the gateway after 2, dropping the 3rd cross-layer message. The fix marks gw_4's forward RTS with RTS_FLAG_RELAY; l5_helper recognises it, skips the originator metric, and emits rts_relay_exempt instead of throttling. Verify: l5_helper emits rts_relay_exempt naming gw_4 as the source, and l5_target still receives the cross-layer traffic.",
